Aim: Write a program to determine the classes of IP Address (A, B, C, D, and E)
Objectives
After completing this experiment, students will be able to:
● Understand IPv4 addressing.
● Identify the different classes of IP addresses.
● Write a Python program to determine the class of an IP address.
● Understand the purpose of each IP address class.
Theory
An IP (Internet Protocol) Address is a unique logical address assigned to every device connected
to a computer network. It allows devices to communicate with each other over a network.
An IPv4 address consists of 32 bits, divided into four octets, each containing 8 bits. The octets
are separated by dots (.).
Each octet can have a value from 0 to 255.
IP Address Classes
IPv4 addresses are classified into five classes based on the value of the first octet.
Class First Octet Range Default Subnet Mask Purpose
A 1 – 126 255.0.0.0 Large networks
B 128 – 191 255.255.0.0 Medium networks
C 192 – 223 255.255.255.0 Small networks
D 224 – 239 Not Applicable Multicasting
E 240 – 255 Not Applicable Experimental
127.x.x.x is reserved for Loopback addresses.
0.x.x.x is reserved for Default Network.
